  "title": "An Exact Hall-Universality Census Through Six Vertices",
  "batch_label": "61",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every integer n with 0 <= n <= 6, including n=0 under the convention fixed in problem.md, every finite simple graph G on the labelled vertex set {1,...,n} is Hall-universal: for every simple graph H on that same labelled set, the Hilton--Johnson Hall inequalities for the graphic lists L_G(v)=N_G(v) imply the existence of a proper L_G-coloring of H. Up to isomorphism the complete positive census has 1, 1, 2, 4, 11, 34, and 156 classes in orders n=0,...,6, and there are no negative classes.",
